# The actual protection against a secret leaking into the image — a
# COPY . . style mistake elsewhere would bake .env into a layer even if
# the application never reads it at runtime. This line is what protects
# against that, not the absence of an ARG/ENV in the Dockerfile alone.
.env
.env.*
.env.local

.git
node_modules
dist

# Demo recordings and dev-only artifacts, not needed at runtime.
demo/
# .dockerignore patterns use Go filepath.Match, which does NOT cross "/" —
# a bare `*.test.ts` only matches root-level files. Every test file in this
# repo lives under src/ (e.g. src/agent/agent.test.ts), so `**/*.test.ts`
# is required for this line to exclude anything at all (code-reviewer
# finding, M3e: the un-globbed version silently excluded zero files).
**/*.test.ts
ISA.md
